# ─── Secrets — NEVER commit these ───────────────────────────────────────────
# Live Google service-account private key. If this ever lands on GitHub the
# Sheet becomes writable by anyone. Keep it local; use the GOOGLE_CREDENTIALS
# GitHub Actions secret in CI instead.
service_account.json
*credentials*.json
*.pem
*.key

# ─── Python ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
__pycache__/
*.pyc
*.pyo
*.pyd
.venv/
venv/
env/
*.egg-info/

# ─── macOS / LibreOffice cruft ──────────────────────────────────────────────
.DS_Store
.~lock*#
.~lock*

# ─── Vestigial local data store (real store is the Google Sheet) ────────────
*.xlsx
*.xls

# ─── Local run artifacts ────────────────────────────────────────────────────
update_log.txt

# NOTE: constants_patch.json is intentionally NOT ignored — it is the payload
# the weekly apply job consumes and must be committed so Actions can see it.
# Applied archives (constants_patch.applied_*.json) and history.json are also
# committed so the Pages history page stays in sync.
news_raw.json
verification_report.json
PROJECT_OVERVIEW.md
